  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Preheat oven to 240°C/220°C fan-forced.\n• Cut beetroot and carrot into small chunks. Cut capsicum into large chunks.\n• Place the veggies, dukkah and a drizzle of olive oil on the lined oven tray. Toss to coat and roast until tender, 20-25 mins.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-64938b3012caf9adcfb73966-2f520683.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Meanwhile, cut haloumi into 1cm slices (you should get 3-4 pieces per person). In a medium bowl, add haloumi and cover with water. Set aside.\n• Finely chop or crush garlic.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-64938b3012caf9adcfb73966-ba806a41.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• In a medium saucepan, melt butter over medium-high heat. Cook garlic until fragrant, 1 min.\n• Add the water and bring to the boil. Add couscous.\n• Stir to combine, cover with a lid and remove from heat.\n• Set aside until water is absorbed, 5 mins. Fluff up with a fork and season to taste. Set aside, uncovered.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-64938b3012caf9adcfb73966-b096029a.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• In a medium frying pan, heat a drizzle of olive oil over medium-high heat. Drain haloumi and pat dry with paper towel and cook until golden brown, 2 mins each side (cook in batches if your pan is getting crowded!).\n• Remove pan from heat, add honey and turn haloumi to coat.\n• Stir roast veggies through garlic couscous.\n• Divide couscous between bowls. Top with haloumi and yoghurt.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-64938b3012caf9adcfb73966-3ef7d260.jpeg"
    }
  ]
